# === captylo.com: downloads and updates (M5) ===
# Goes inside the existing captylo.com { ... } block, before its file_server line.
#
# The DMGs live in their own folder (PUBLISH_DOWNLOADS in deploy/local.env), outside the site's
# web root: the site deploy syncs site/ with --delete and would remove them otherwise. That
# folder has to be visible inside the Caddy container; replace DOWNLOADS_DIR below with its
# path as the container sees it (check with "test -d" inside the container).
# Only *.dmg goes there, so captylo.com/download/ (site/download/index.html) stays a site page.
# Captylo.dmg is a relative symlink to the newest Captylo-<version>.dmg (scripts/publish-release.sh).
    @dmg path /download/*.dmg
    handle @dmg {
        uri strip_prefix /download
        root * DOWNLOADS_DIR
        header Cache-Control "no-cache"
        # Caddy has no type for .dmg and would send none
        header Content-Type "application/x-apple-diskimage"
        file_server
    }
    # The appcast and the release notes come from the site itself (site/updates/), never cached,
    # so Sparkle sees a new release as soon as it is published.
    header /updates/* Cache-Control "no-cache"
# === /captylo.com: downloads and updates ===
